# File: hooks/register.test.ts, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute-supervisor.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/dual-surface-contract.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/638-run-interactive-commands-in-claude-desktop-and-remote-sessions-and-dispose-of-finished-sdlc-execute-stage-workers/requirements.md
Feature: Run interactive commands in Claude Desktop and remote sessions, and dispose of finished /sdlc-execute stage workers

  @SCN001
  Scenario: An interactive command runs in a Claude Desktop session
    Given a session whose start reported isInteractive false
    And whose surface roster is "desktop" when the command runs
    When "/sdlc-draft-issue" runs
    Then its workflow is rendered, "/plan" runs, and the workflow is submitted as the person's prompt
    And "Run /sdlc-draft-issue in the TUI." is not printed

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: An interactive command runs in a remotely attached session
    Given a session whose surface roster is "<roster>" when the command runs
    When an interactive "/sdlc-*" command runs
    Then its workflow is rendered, "/plan" runs, and the workflow is submitted as the person's prompt

    Examples:
      | roster          |
      | terminal,mobile |
      | mobile          |

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A headless session keeps refusing interactive commands
    Given a session whose surface roster is empty when the command runs
    When "/sdlc-draft-issue" runs
    Then it answers "Run /sdlc-draft-issue in the TUI." with exit code 2
    And no workflow is rendered

  @SCN004
  Scenario: A finished stage worker is stopped before the next stage starts
    Given an execute run whose implement worker wrote a passed handoff with no redispatch or halt decision
    When the controller advances to verify
    Then the implement worker is stopped before the verify worker is spawned
    And the implement worker's agent record has "stopped" true

  @SCN005
  Scenario Outline: No worker outlives its run
    Given an execute run that ends by <ending>
    When the controller records the run's result
    Then every stage worker the run spawned was stopped
    And none is listed as pending, running or waiting

    Examples:
      | ending  |
      | success |
      | failure |
      | halt    |

  @SCN006
  Scenario: An unconfirmed stop is reported, not hidden
    Given a stage worker whose stop cannot be confirmed
    When the controller finishes that stage
    Then the stop is attempted once more
    And the run fails with "worker_stop_failed"
    And the recorded run result includes "stage worker <agentId>: stop not confirmed"

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Every hooks-module command works on both the CLI and Desktop
    Given each command the hooks module registers
    When it runs once with a "terminal" roster and once with a "desktop" roster
    Then both runs reach the same workflow submission
    And the commands exercised are exactly the registered commands

  @SCN008
  Scenario: UI degrades gracefully on a terminal-only roster
    Given a hooks-module path that shows a toast
    When the session's roster is "terminal" only
    Then the command reaches the same outcome as on a "desktop" roster without an error
    And the hooks module calls no "$.ui" member other than "toast" and "log"

  @SCN009
  Scenario: The project states the dual-surface rule
    Given the repository after this change
    When "CLAUDE.md" and "steering/snippets/project-product.md" are read
    Then "CLAUDE.md" has a "Desktop and CLI" section stating both surfaces are supported, Desktop may offer richer UI, and the CLI degrades gracefully
    And the Product Principles and Intent Verification tables each have a "Desktop and CLI" row
